-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre at good points, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a field extension $F/K$ a *place* of $F$ over $K$ (`Place K F`) is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose lattice of ideals is principal; `Place.ord` is the associated normalised additive valuation, `Place.IsRational` says that $K$ surjects onto the residue field, and `Place.evalAt` is the resulting $K$-valued evaluation map.
--
--   **Base data.** A prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q = 3$; a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of the level-$M'$ geometric function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with the hypothesis `hW` that membership in $W$ is equivalent to membership in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$, that is, to being a rational affine geometric place at which the generic $j$-invariant evaluates into the supersingular set $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$; and the inclusion `hle` of the base-changed full level-$M'$ field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** A datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the upper field, a surjective ring map `R₀.residue` onto the characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees, compatibility of `R₀.integers` and `R₀.residue` with $A$ and its residue map, the scaling property that every non-zero element can be multiplied into `R₀.integers` with non-zero residue, and compatibility of `placeMap` with orders of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, this element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The Igusa family.** A primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by the projective line $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings indexed by $W$. The hypothesis `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as the Gauss-type ring: $f$ belongs to it exactly when there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ non-zero and $f \cdot \bar y = \bar x$ after coefficientwise inclusion of $A$ into $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The hypothesis `hIg` says that each line $\ell$ is reached from $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ by some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ through the reduction map $\mathrm{redQ}\,q$, with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pull-back of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; `hIg_perm` asserts that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pull-back along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   **The supersingular rings.** `hSS_A`: for each $s \in W$, an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ (after the structure map) if and only if it lies in $A$. `hSS_over`: for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ holds at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$, $j$ being the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,(\mathrm{jq})$, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the evaluation at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference $f - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pull-back along every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   **The regular prolongation.** A datum $R$ of type `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') (xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M'))` — a valuation subring with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and with the scaling property — subject to `hR`: `R.integers` $= O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O`: $f \in$ `R₀.integers` if and only if its image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   **Ramification and constants.** An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; together with `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The finite layer.** A finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ cut out by $A$ (i.e. $x \in A_1 \iff x \in A$), which is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   With $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is the following. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ satisfying: the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every finite family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ together with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Put $T_1$ for the $k_0$-subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ generated by the image of $K_1$ together with $F_0$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions, i.e. the image of $a \in A_1$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $j_1 \in T_1$ be non-zero and equal, in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, to the image of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,(\mathrm{jq})$ under the inclusion `hle`. Write $\mathfrak X_1 = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_1\,T_1\,j_1$ for the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two affine charts $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ in $T_1$ and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with the structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and the chart morphisms $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}, \iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$.
--
--   The statement introduces, by `let`, the following predicates on points $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and elements $f \in T_1$. `InStalk x f`: for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = x$ there are $g, h$ in the chart algebra with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, and likewise on $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$. `InMax x f`: the same, with the additional requirement $g \in y$. `Centred P x`, for $P$ a place of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational and for every $f$ with `InStalk x f` one has $f \in P$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ has $A$-valuation $< 1$ exactly when `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x`: $\mathrm{toBase}(x)$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for each $y$ over $x$ in either chart, every chart element whose image lies in the non-units of `R.integers` lies in $y$; and for each $y$ over $x$ in $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1) \notin \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$. `Reads x Q`, for $Q$ a place of the reduced level-$q^2M'$ field: for every $f$ with `InStalk x f`, $f$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in $Q$, and that residue is a non-unit of $Q$ exactly when `InMax x f`. `OffBranch x`: for every line $\ell \ne \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ and every $y$ over $x$ in either chart there is a chart element whose image lies in the non-units of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$. Of these, only `GoodPt` occurs in the conclusion; `Centred`, `Reads` and `OffBranch` are defined but not used in it.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, every $\varpi_1 \in A_1$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_1$, and every element $\varpi_x$ of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_1$ at $x$ that is the germ at $x$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi_1$ by the global-sections map of $\mathrm{toBase}$ (through the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism for $A_1$), the quotient ring
--   $$\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_1, x} / (\varpi_x)$$
--   is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case of the regularity of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the level-$q^2M'$ modular curve over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$, at points lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and away from supersingular $j$-invariants; the proof reduces to the two fibre-regularity results for the Gauss valuation subring, in the cases of a point on the finite chart with maximal prime and of a cuspidal point off that chart. It feeds the identification of the place read off at a good point and the off-branch property of good points, which together with the companion case $q \ge 5$ supply the local input for the semistable covering of the modular curve.
